doc:sch-2-sec-372-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "372(1) 1A  Dealing in identification information that involves use of a" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:  (a) the first person deals in identification information; and  (b) the first person does so using a carriage service; and  (c) the first person intends that any person (the user) (whether or not the first person) will use the identification information to pretend to be, or to pass the user off as, another person (whether living, dead, real or fictitious) for the purpose of:  (i) committing an offence; or  (ii) facilitating the commission of an offence; and  (d) the offence referred to in paragraph (c) is:  (i) an indictable offence against a law of the Commonwealth; or  (ii) an indictable offence against a law of a State or Territory; or  (iii) a foreign indictable offence. Penalty: Imprisonment for 5 years. Note: Deal, in identification information, includes make, supply or use any such information. See section 370.1." ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-372-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "372(2) 1A  Dealing in identification information that involves use of a"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-372-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Absolute liability applies to the paragraphs (1)(b) and (d) elements of the offence. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167  Identity crime and air travel  Schedule 2 Identity crime  Part 1  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012 No. 167, 2012            21 Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. Dealing in identification information obtained using a carriage service" ;
