    cof:title "3UM(3) Identity information at airports—requirements" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The constable may request the suspect to give the constable evidence of the suspect’s identity by:  (a) producing a government photographic identity document issued in relation to the suspect, if held by the suspect; and  (b) if the suspect does not produce a government photographic identity document as requested under paragraph (a)— producing another identity document in relation to the suspect, if held by the suspect; and  (c) if the suspect does not produce an identity document as requested under paragraph (a) or (b)—giving the constable the suspect’s name and address. Constable’s duties" ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-3um-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3UM(4) Identity information at airports—requirements"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-3um-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) The constable must, before making a request under subsection (3):  (a) if the constable is not in uniform: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167  Identity crime and air travel  Schedule 2 False identity and air travel  Part 2  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012 No. 167, 2012            25  (i) show the suspect evidence that the constable is a constable; and  (ii) if the suspect requests—comply with subsection (5); and  (b) in any case—inform the suspect that it may be an offence not to comply with the request, or to give the constable a false or misleading document, or false or misleading information, in response to the request." ;
    skos:definition "(4) The constable must, before making a request under subsection (3):  (a) if the constable is not in uniform: ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167  Identity crime and air travel  Schedule 2 False identity and air travel  Part 2  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012 No. 167, 2012            25  (i) show the suspect evidence that the constable is a constable; and  (ii) if the suspect requests—comply with subsection (5); and  (b) in any case—inform the suspect that it may be an offence not to comply with the request, or to give the constable a false or misleading document, or false or misleading information, in response to the request."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4490216fc17f9799c845d64593459cca89fb2f60e71fdcfbfc4a2db1d825a3d4" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-3um ;
    cof:pageNumber "28"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Constable must provide identity information before making a request." ;
    dc:description "constable evidence, suspect's response to the request" ;
