concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-26 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "26 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-26 ;
    values:originalText "Offence by constable  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection 3UM(4); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the conduct breaches the requirement. Penalty: 5 penalty units.  (4) In this section: engage in conduct means:  (a) do an act; or  (b) omit to perform an act. Criminal Code Act 1995" ;
    skos:definition "Offence by constable  (3) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person is subject to a requirement under subsection 3UM(4); and  (b) the person engages in conduct; and  (c) the conduct breaches the requirement. Penalty: 5 penalty units.  (4) In this section: engage in conduct means:  (a) do an act; or  (b) omit to perform an act. Criminal Code Act 1995"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d43688271ebd2ed4fd848b440f659c39a82e0f9fc22398ebb1a00ae254bf765e" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer ;
