doc:sch-2-sec-376 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "376 1  Definitions for Division 376" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "In this Division: air passenger ticket, for a flight, means a ticket, or electronic record, on the basis of which a person is treated as being entitled to travel as a passenger on:  (a) the flight; or  (b) a journey that includes the flight. false: identification information relating to a person is false if it is false in a material particular that affects the capacity of the information to be used (whether alone or in conjunction with other information or documents) to identify the person. Note: For the meaning of identification information, see section 370.1. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167  Identity crime and air travel  Schedule 2 False identity and air travel  Part 2  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012 No. 167, 2012            27" ;
    cof:pageNumber "30"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-376-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "376 2  False identification information—at constitutional airports"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-376-2 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the defendant) commits an offence if:  (a) the defendant uses information at a place; and  (b) the defendant does so reckless as to whether the information is used to identify the defendant as a passenger on a flight; and  (c) the information is identification information; and  (d) the information is false in relation to the defendant; and  (e) the place is a constitutional airport. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.  (2) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(e). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2.  (3) In this section: constitutional airport means:  (a) a Commonwealth aerodrome within the meaning of the Crimes (Aviation) Act 1991 (see section 3 of that Act); or  (b) another airport, if the airport is in a Territory." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person (the defendant) commits an offence if:  (a) the defendant uses information at a place; and  (b) the defendant does so reckless as to whether the information is used to identify the defendant as a passenger on a flight; and  (c) the information is identification information; and  (d) the information is false in relation to the defendant; and  (e) the place is a constitutional airport. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.  (2) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(e). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2.  (3) In this section: constitutional airport means:  (a) a Commonwealth aerodrome within the meaning of the Crimes (Aviation) Act 1991 (see section 3 of that Act); or  (b) another airport, if the airport is in a Territory."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "682ca5840dd343f5d1bbee9e2ed89fbfc5151166def67b8549ff581e3ad58b94" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-376-2-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-376-2-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-376-2-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012.pdf, p.31" .
doc:sch-2-sec-376-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "376 2  False identification information—at constitutional airports" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person (the defendant) commits an offence if:  (a) the defendant uses information at a place; and  (b) the defendant does so reckless as to whether the information is used to identify the defendant as a passenger on a flight; and  (c) the information is identification information; and  (d) the information is false in relation to the defendant; and  (e) the place is a constitutional airport. Penalty: Imprisonment for 12 months.  (2) Absolute liability applies to paragraph (1)(e). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2.  (3) In this section: constitutional airport means:  (a) a Commonwealth aerodrome within the meaning of the Crimes (Aviation) Act 1991 (see section 3 of that Act); or  (b) another airport, if the airport is in a Territory." ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer .

