doc:sch-2-sec-28-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "28(3) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures)" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) In a prosecution for an offence against subsection (1) or (2), if the prosecution proves beyond reasonable doubt that an air passenger ticket was obtained, then it is presumed, unless the defendant proves to the contrary, that a carriage service was used to obtain the ticket. Note: A defendant bears a legal burden in relation to the matter in this subsection: see section 13.4." ;
    cof:pageNumber "32"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-28-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "28(4) Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-28-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) Absolute liability applies to paragraphs (1)(e) and (f) and (2)(e) and (f). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167  Identity crime and air travel  Schedule 2 False identity and air travel  Part 2  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012 No. 167, 2012            29" ;
    skos:definition "(4) Absolute liability applies to paragraphs (1)(e) and (f) and (2)(e) and (f). Note: For absolute liability, see section 6.2. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2012A00167  Identity crime and air travel  Schedule 2 False identity and air travel  Part 2  Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures) Act 2012 No. 167, 2012            29"@en ;
