concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-serious-drugs-identity-crime-and-other-measures-act-2012-sch-2-sec-30 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "30 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Serious Drugs, Identity Crime and Other Measures)"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-30 ;
    values:originalText "(4) In this section: constitutional flight means:  (a) a flight that starts or ends in a Territory; or  (b) a flight between Australia and a foreign country in which an aircraft is used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage of passengers; or  (c) a flight between one State and another State in which an aircraft is used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage of passengers." ;
    skos:definition "(4) In this section: constitutional flight means:  (a) a flight that starts or ends in a Territory; or  (b) a flight between Australia and a foreign country in which an aircraft is used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage of passengers; or  (c) a flight between one State and another State in which an aircraft is used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage of passengers."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "37d71f1f1f4dcf0ceaf863f26db53bca084ba2fb75f7d33068bf4ba06776f8ed" ;
    cof:pageNumber "34"^^xsd:integer ;
